From: meenmachine1 <78238681+meenmachine1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:40:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Decompiler: fail cleanly when an INDIRECT's effect op was
 removed before merging

Merge::snipReads and Merge::trimOpOutput insert a COPY after the op that
causes an INDIRECT (PcodeOp::getOpFromConst of the INDIRECT's iop input).
That op can already be dead: SplitDatatype::splitCopy (RuleSplitCopy, in the
late cleanup pool) destroys the COPY it splits, and when that COPY is a STORE
that RuleStoreVarnode turned into a COPY, INDIRECTs still name it as their
effect. No RuleIndirectCollapse runs after the cleanup pool, so the INDIRECT
reaches ActionMergeRequired; Funcdata::opInsertAfter then dereferences the
dead op's null parent block and the decompiler segfaults.

Check that the effect op is still alive and throw a LowlevelError instead,
so the function fails with an error and the process survives. Only
functions that crashed before are affected.

Seen on: Mbed TLS 3.6.2 x86-64 gcc -O2 (mbedtls_aria_self_test). Ghidra
12.1.4's decompiler process dies on the same function.
Repro: decomp_dbg, restore the attached debug XML, load function
mbedtls_aria_self_test, decompile.

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/merge.cc b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/merge.cc
index c416820..ec442c9 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/merge.cc
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/merge.cc
@@ -465,6 +465,8 @@ void Merge::snipReads(Varnode *vn,list<PcodeOp *> &markedop)
     else
       afterop = vn->getDef();
   }
+  if (afterop != (PcodeOp *)0 && afterop->isDead())
+    throw LowlevelError("Cannot snip reads: op causing INDIRECT effect has been removed");
   copyop = allocateCopyTrim(vn, pc, markedop.front());
   if (afterop == (PcodeOp *)0)
     data.opInsertBegin(copyop,bl);
@@ -664,6 +666,8 @@ void Merge::trimOpOutput(PcodeOp *op)
     afterop = PcodeOp::getOpFromConst(op->getIn(1)->getAddr()); // Insert copyop AFTER source of indirect
   else
     afterop = op;
+  if (afterop->isDead())
+    throw LowlevelError("Cannot trim output: op causing INDIRECT effect has been removed");
   vn = op->getOut();
   Datatype *ct = vn->getType();
   copyop = data.newOp(1,op->getAddr());
